The early-exit guard calls `doPayload(listener)` (which invokes `listener.onResponse(...)`) but does **not** return. Execution falls through to the rest of `tumbleWindow`, which eventually calls `checkMissingEvents(() -> advance(c, listener), listener)` — using the same listener a second time. This will cause a double-response (or an `IllegalStateException` from the `ActionListener` implementation) whenever `allowPartialSequenceResults == false` and shard failures are present.
```java
if (allowPartialSequenceResults == false && shardFailures.isEmpty() == false) {
    doPayload(listener);
    return;  // <-- missing
}
```

